    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1960-p28.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "For \\(x\\ne3,\\) subtracting the identical fractions from both sides leaves \\(x=3.\\) But \\(x=3\\) makes the original denominators zero, so it is not in the domain. The equation has no root.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is B.",
      "hints": [
        "The identical fractional terms cancel wherever the equation is defined",
        "Check whether the resulting value lies in the original domain"
      ],
